[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819073124","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105622#issuecomment-2819073124","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105622","id":2819073124,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oB6Rk","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T17:26:28Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T17:26:28Z","body":"I think this is unavoidable, reimporting the texture regenerates it and recreates the data, and in other cases where you manually change the texture I'd say this would be expected. I'd say this should be handled by responding to the reimport by generating the dependent texture again","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819073124/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819089180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105622#issuecomment-2819089180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105622","id":2819089180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oB-Mc","user":{"login":"mr11stein","id":149411461,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOfWhQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149411461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein","html_url":"https://github.com/mr11stein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T17:34:37Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T17:34:37Z","body":"But the whole point of using RIDs is to enable swapping the underlying data opaquely no? Also, what you suggest may not be feasible since you'd have to free the old dependent resources (like uniform sets) which may still be used by the renderer when the change is detected. If you write a plugin or something where you can supply a Texture2D from outside, your plugin now has to track the resource or it will fail. I think this is a proper bug.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819089180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819106415","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105622#issuecomment-2819106415","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105622","id":2819106415,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oCCZv","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T17:42:34Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T17:42:34Z","body":"RIDs are designed to use the same resource, but a reimported asset isn't the same resource, and there's reasons to keep the old RID valid in the background, that is still a valid resource, so replacing it would be potentially breaking things. The underlying data *isn't* the same when reimporting, so it'd IMO be weird to keep the same RID for that (and not keep that RID for the old resource for anything still using it)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819106415/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819117456","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105622#issuecomment-2819117456","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105622","id":2819117456,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oCFGQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T17:48:11Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T17:48:11Z","body":"> But the whole point of using RIDs is to enable swapping the underlying data opaquely no?\n\nNo, this is not a goal of RIDs at all. RIDs give you a handle into a resource in another system. They are a way to access low-level features without having ownership of the underlying data. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819117456/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819140472","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105622#issuecomment-2819140472","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105622","id":2819140472,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oCKt4","user":{"login":"mr11stein","id":149411461,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOfWhQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149411461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein","html_url":"https://github.com/mr11stein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T18:00:27Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T18:00:27Z","body":"Got it, but at the very least there should be some way to handle this gracefully right? The engine pulling the texture from under my ass and breaking everything when the rendering device hasn't freed the data is still a bug imo.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819140472/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819147249","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105622#issuecomment-2819147249","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105622","id":2819147249,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oCMXx","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T18:03:49Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T18:03:49Z","body":"The problem is you are caching the RID handle even after it has been destroyed. RID handles are not resources that you should be caching. Its up to you to manage the lifetime of your resources. If you have a resource that can go out of scope one frame, then you need to retrieve the handle each frame.\n\n> There are 2 hard problems in computer science: cache invalidation, naming things, and off-by-1 errors.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819147249/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819237439","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105622#issuecomment-2819237439","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105622","id":2819237439,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6oCiY_","user":{"login":"mr11stein","id":149411461,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOfWhQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149411461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein","html_url":"https://github.com/mr11stein","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mr11stein/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-21T18:43:58Z","updated_at":"2025-04-21T18:43:58Z","body":"Understood, I'll close this then. I still think there's an uncanny mismatch when using an engine managed resource in an environment where everything is manually managed, but that's an API or documentation problem, not a bug.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2819237439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]